{
  "_readme": "Every relic in the game. Edit this file, then run Prince's Palace > Build Default Content. RELICS ARE DRAFTED PER RUN: three are offered at the start of a descent, the player keeps one for that run only, and it is gone when the run ends — nothing here is permanent progression. The exception is a relic with draftable: false (kinship), which is never offered in a draft or the shop and only arrives through an event's relic effect, still for that run only; its rarity sets only its colour band. rarity is an AUTHORED statement about how often the relic should be offered — unlike item rarity it is not derived from a tier, because a relic has no numbers to derive it from; changing a relic's band is this one word and nothing else. effects lists what a relic does: stat kinds and at most one mechanic, each an EffectKind name with its headline magnitude (a flag mechanic authors none). OMIT effects for a relic that has no behaviour yet. A mechanic must be unique across relics: two relics doing the same thing makes one of them a dead choice in a draft; stat-only and empty relics are exempt. Field-by-field documentation, defaults and valid enum values: docs/CONTENT_SCHEMA.md.",
  "_placeholders": "forest_wardens_tooth is DELIBERATELY MECHANIC-LESS -- it exists so the draft, the rarity ladder and the glossary can be seen working against a pool big enough to be a real choice, before anybody has designed what it does. It is the only one left; every other relic that used to sit in this state (seven_teeth through drowned_lantern) has since earned `effects`. Give it some when it earns one; until then it is honest about being furniture. Of the 20 relics from balance pass 2 (magic_marker through phoenix_egg), loaded_dice and dancers_anklet still point iconPath at Assets/_Project/Art/Generated/disc_metal.png -- a baked metallic-coin placeholder (see ProceduralSpriteBaker) -- until each earns real art from Art/Items/Relics/Processed/; the other eighteen already have it. None of the 20 are mechanic-less, only unillustrated.",
